<https://github.com/john1hsu/salesforce-knowledge-graph/id/oauth-2-0> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The IETF authorization framework (RFC 6749, with bearer-token usage in RFC 6750) that lets a client application obtain limited, scoped access tokens to a protected resource on behalf of a resource owner or itself, without handling the owner's password; it underpins Salesforce API authorization, and its security guidance is now consolidated in RFC 9700 and the in-progress OAuth 2.1 draft." .
